From b66b2ddfd1e14e157816f8a1f9cc8e5737ae49e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HiGarfield <HiGarfield@126.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 10:52:07 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] perf(stdio): use memrchr for line-buffered fwrite

__fwritex scans backwards byte by byte to find the last newline in a
line-buffered block. Long blocks with the newline near the start make
that scan dominate the write itself. Use the hidden __memrchr helper,
which now scans words instead.

Scope:
- src/stdio/fwrite.c only; the newline search and the split point are
  otherwise unchanged.
- The direct-write path for blocks larger than the buffer is untouched.

Risk:
- __memrchr is a hidden libc symbol, available in both static and
  dynamic builds; no new public API is used.
- Search character stays '\\n', matching the original behavior even
  if lbf were set to another value.
- The pre-existing sign-compare warning in this file is unchanged.

Performance (x86_64, gcc 16, -Os, 256 KiB line-buffered block,
cookie writer that only counts bytes, median of 9 runs):
- 234.8 -> 55.7 us/call (4.2x)

Correctness:
- Cookie-stream verifier: 3000 cases with varied buffer sizes,
  newline positions and chunk lengths; byte stream and length match.
- tmpfile line-buffered round trip passes.
- 32-bit i386 static build, valgrind clean, gcc/clang strict compile
  with only the pre-existing sign-compare warning.
---
 src/stdio/fwrite.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/stdio/fwrite.c b/src/stdio/fwrite.c
index 7a567b2..3126e7c 100644
--- a/src/stdio/fwrite.c
+++ b/src/stdio/fwrite.c
@@ -10,8 +10,10 @@ size_t __fwritex(const unsigned char *restrict s, size_t l, FILE *restrict f)
 	if (l > f->wend - f->wpos) return f->write(f, s, l);
 
 	if (f->lbf >= 0) {
-		/* Match /^(.*\n|)/ */
-		for (i=l; i && s[i-1] != '\n'; i--);
+		/* Match /^(.*\n|)/. The word-at-a-time reverse scan avoids
+		 * walking long line-buffered blocks one byte at a time. */
+		const unsigned char *z = __memrchr(s, '\n', l);
+		i = z ? (size_t)(z - s) + 1 : 0;
 		if (i) {
 			size_t n = f->write(f, s, i);
 			if (n < i) return n;
-- 
2.43.0

